IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wpa-types`
IMPORT `wpa-deductions`

-- Wages Protection Act 1983 — GOALS 3 AND 4: RECOVERY, PREMIUMS, SPENDING,
-- PENALTIES.
--
--   Goal 3: "What may the worker, or a Labour Inspector, recover from the
--            employer under s 11, and is the action in time? What may be
--            recovered from a person involved (s 11A)?"
--   Goal 4: "Was a premium charged for employment (s 12A), or a requirement
--            imposed on how wages are spent (s 12); who is liable to a
--            penalty, and who may recover it (s 13)?"
--
-- Source: ../source/WPA1983.txt — ss 11, 11A, 12, 12A, 13; Schedule.

§ `Goal 3 — recovery`

§§ `Recovery of deductions from the employer (s 11(1)(a))`

-- s 11(1)(a) a worker or Labour Inspector may recover "any deduction made
-- (otherwise than pursuant to section 6) ... if— (i) that deduction was not
-- consented to, or requested by, that worker in writing; or (ii) the making
-- of that deduction was consented to, or requested by, that worker in
-- writing; but the consent or request concerned was obtained by threat of
-- dismissal, or otherwise by duress; or (iii) the making of that deduction
-- was in accordance with a general deductions clause in that worker's
-- employment agreement but that worker was not consulted before that
-- deduction was made; or (iv) that deduction was unreasonable".
--
-- Grounds (iii) and (iv) were inserted on 27 November 2025 by the Statutes
-- Amendment Act 2025. FORK F3: they reach deductions made on or after that
-- day only (the Act states no transitional rule; legislation does not have
-- retrospective effect). FORK F4: a deduction relying on s 6 that does not
-- meet s 6(3) is not made "pursuant to section 6", and was not consented to,
-- so ground (i) applies. FORK F5: a consent withdrawn under s 5(2) does not
-- cover deductions after the s 5(2) day, so ground (i) applies to them.
-- FORK F6: s 15 and s 16 deductions are not recoverable — the Act is read
-- subject to other Acts, and does not derogate from collective agreements
-- or orders. A consented deduction that is not for a lawful purpose breaches
-- s 4 but is not within (i)-(iv).
@ref s 11(1)(a); ss 5(2), 6, 15, 16
GIVEN d IS A Deduction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deduction is within s 11(1)(a)` d IF
    CONSIDER d's `basis`
    WHEN `the worker's written consent` general duress THEN
            duress
        OR  NOT `the consent or request still covers what is done on` (d's `made on`) `, notice` (d's `notice of withdrawal`)
        OR  (    `the grounds inserted in 2025 reach a deduction on` (d's `made on`)
             AND (   (general AND NOT d's `the worker was consulted before the deduction`)
                  OR d's `unreasonable`))
    WHEN `the worker's written request` duress THEN
            duress
        OR  NOT `the consent or request still covers what is done on` (d's `made on`) `, notice` (d's `notice of withdrawal`)
        OR  (`the grounds inserted in 2025 reach a deduction on` (d's `made on`) AND d's `unreasonable`)
    WHEN `recovery of an overpayment under s 6` o THEN NOT `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` o
    WHEN `required or authorised by another Act (s 15)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a collective agreement or an order of the Court or Authority (s 16)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no written consent or request` THEN TRUE

-- The amount within s 11(1)(a). For a deduction that meets s 6, the part
-- above the overpayment is not "pursuant to section 6" and was not consented
-- to: ground (i).
@ref s 11(1)(a); s 6(2)
GIVEN d IS A Deduction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part of the deduction within s 11(1)(a)` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d's `basis`
    WHEN `recovery of an overpayment under s 6` o THEN
        IF `the employer may recover the overpayment under s 6` o
        THEN max 0 (d's `amount` MINUS o's `amount`)
        ELSE d's `amount`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the deduction is within s 11(1)(a)` d THEN d's `amount` ELSE 0

@ref s 11(1)(a)(iii)-(iv); Statutes Amendment Act 2025 s 157
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grounds inserted in 2025 reach a deduction on` d IF
    d AT LEAST Date 27 11 2025

§§ `Time limits (s 11(2)-(3))`

-- s 11(2) "No action under subsection (1) shall be brought after the
-- expiration of 6 years from the date on which the cause of action
-- concerned arose." FORK F7: the period runs from the day after the cause
-- arose, so an action brought on the sixth anniversary is in time.
-- s 11(3) "No such action shall be brought in respect of any cause of action
-- that arose more than 2 years before the commencement of this Act"
-- (1 February 1984, s 1(2)).
@ref s 11(2)-(3); s 1(2)
GIVEN arose IS A DATE, brought IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action under s 11 is in time, cause arose` arose `, brought` brought IF
        brought AT MOST `add years` arose 6
    AND arose AT LEAST Date 1 2 1982

-- The amount recoverable under s 11(1)(a) for one deduction, in an action
-- brought on the day given. A deduction before 1 April 2016 is refused (the
-- Act as it then stood is not carried; any such action is in any case out
-- of time under s 11(2) by 1 April 2022).
@ref s 11(1)(a), (2), (3); Schedule cl 2
GIVEN d IS A Deduction, brought IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount recoverable under s 11(1)(a) for` d `, action brought` brought MEANS
    IF NOT `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` (d's `made on`)
    THEN IF `an action under s 11 is in time, cause arose` (d's `made on`) `, brought` brought
         THEN `conduct before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 Act, which this encoding does not carry`
         ELSE 0
    ELSE IF `an action under s 11 is in time, cause arose` (d's `made on`) `, brought` brought
         THEN `the part of the deduction within s 11(1)(a)` d
         ELSE 0

@ref s 11(1)(a)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`conduct before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 Act, which this encoding does not carry` MEANS
    REFUSE "conduct before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 Act, which this encoding does not carry"

§§ `Recovery from a person involved (s 11A)`

-- s 11A(1)-(2), (5): the same scheme as the Minimum Wage Act 1983 s 11AA.
-- "(2) ... only,— (a) in the case of recovery by a worker, with the prior
-- leave of the Authority or court; and (b) to the extent that the worker's
-- employer is unable to pay the wages." s 11A was inserted by the 2016 Act
-- and does not reach earlier conduct (Schedule cl 2(2)).
@ref s 11A(1), (2), (5); Schedule cl 2
@export How much a worker or a Labour Inspector may recover from a person who is not the employer under s 11A(1)-(2) of the Wages Protection Act 1983 (NZ): the arrears of wages the employer is unable to pay, if the worker is entitled to them under the Act, they are unpaid due to non-compliance, and the person is involved (ERA s 142W); a worker needs the prior leave of the Authority or court. 0 when the section does not allow recovery. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN claimant IS A Claimant  @desc Who seeks to recover: the worker, a Labour Inspector, or someone else
      a IS AN `Arrears claim against a person involved`  @desc The claim: entitlement, non-compliance, involvement, leave, the unpaid wages, what the employer can pay, and when the conduct occurred
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the arrears recoverable under s 11A by` claimant `on` a MEANS
    IF     `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` (a's `date of the conduct`)
       AND (claimant EQUALS `a Labour Inspector` OR (claimant EQUALS `the worker` AND a's `prior leave of the Authority or court`))
       AND NOT a's `the person is the worker's employer`
       AND a's `the worker is entitled to the wages under this Act`
       AND a's `the wages are unpaid due to non-compliance with this Act`
       AND a's `the person is involved in the non-compliance`
    THEN max 0 (a's `unpaid wages` MINUS a's `what the employer is able to pay`)
    ELSE 0

§ `Goal 4 — premiums, spending, penalties`

§§ `Premiums for employment (ss 12A, 11A(3)-(4))`

-- s 12A(1) "No employer or person engaged on behalf of the employer shall
-- seek or receive any premium in respect of the employment of any person,
-- whether the premium is sought or received from the person employed or
-- proposed to be employed or from any other person." ("or person engaged on
-- behalf of the employer" was added in 2016: Schedule cl 2(2).)
@ref s 12A(1); Schedule cl 2
GIVEN `sought or received by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN, `sought or received by a person engaged on the employer's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12A(1) is breached` `sought or received by the employer` `sought or received by a person engaged on the employer's behalf` `the date of the conduct` MEANS
        `sought or received by the employer`
    OR  (`sought or received by a person engaged on the employer's behalf` AND `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` `the date of the conduct`)

-- s 12A(2) "the person by whom the money was paid or, as the case may be,
-- from whose wages it was deducted, may recover that amount from the
-- employer as a debt due to the person; and civil proceedings ... may be
-- instituted ... by the person or ... by a Labour Inspector ... on behalf of
-- the person." It reaches money the EMPLOYER receives.
@ref s 12A(2)
GIVEN claimant IS A Claimant, `received by the employer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the premium recoverable from the employer under s 12A(2) by` claimant `, received by the employer` `received by the employer` MEANS
    IF claimant EQUALS `the person who paid the premium or from whose wages it was deducted` OR claimant EQUALS `a Labour Inspector`
    THEN `received by the employer`
    ELSE 0

-- s 11A(3) "A Labour Inspector, worker, or person concerned may recover from
-- a person involved in non-compliance with section 12A any premium paid in
-- breach of that section." (4) "only,— (a) in the case of recovery by a
-- worker or person concerned, with the prior leave of the Authority or
-- court; and (b) to the extent that the employer concerned is unable to pay
-- the premium." s 11A was inserted by the 2016 Act and does not reach
-- earlier conduct (Schedule cl 2(2)).
@ref s 11A(3)-(5); Schedule cl 2
GIVEN claimant IS A Claimant, involved IS A BOOLEAN, leave IS A BOOLEAN, premium IS A NUMBER, `the employer is able to pay` IS A NUMBER, `the conduct occurred on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the premium recoverable from a person involved under s 11A(3) by` claimant `, involved:` involved `, leave:` leave `, premium` premium `, the employer can pay` `the employer is able to pay` `, conduct on` `the conduct occurred on` MEANS
    IF     `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` `the conduct occurred on`
       AND involved
       AND (   claimant EQUALS `a Labour Inspector`
            OR ((claimant EQUALS `the worker` OR claimant EQUALS `the person who paid the premium or from whose wages it was deducted`) AND leave))
    THEN max 0 (premium MINUS `the employer is able to pay`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `Spending of wages (s 12)`

-- s 12 "No employer shall impose any requirement on any worker as to any
-- place or manner in which or any person with whom that worker shall expend
-- wages received by that worker, or dismiss any worker on account of any
-- place or manner in which or any person with whom that worker expends
-- those wages."
@ref s 12
GIVEN `imposed a requirement on where, how or with whom wages are spent` IS A BOOLEAN, `dismissed the worker on account of how wages were spent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12 is breached` `imposed a requirement on where, how or with whom wages are spent` `dismissed the worker on account of how wages were spent` IF
        `imposed a requirement on where, how or with whom wages are spent`
    OR  `dismissed the worker on account of how wages were spent`

§§ `Penalties (s 13)`

-- s 13(1) "Where— (a) any payment is made by or on behalf of any employer in
-- contravention of this Act; or (b) any employer or any person on that
-- employer's behalf contravenes or fails to comply with any of the
-- provisions of this Act,— that employer, and every person involved in the
-- contravention or failure, is liable to a penalty imposed under the
-- Employment Relations Act 2000 by the Employment Relations Authority."
-- (3): "involved" is ERA s 142W, an input. s 13(1) was amended in 2016;
-- earlier conduct is refused.
@ref s 13(1), (3); Schedule cl 2
@export Whether a person is liable to a penalty under s 13 of the Wages Protection Act 1983 (NZ): where a payment is made by or for the employer in contravention of the Act, or the employer or a person on its behalf contravenes or fails to comply with it, the employer and every person involved (ERA s 142W) are liable to a penalty imposed by the Employment Relations Authority. Conduct before 1 April 2016 is outside the section as it now stands. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN `there was a contravention or failure by or for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc s 13(1)(a)-(b): a payment in contravention of the Act, or a contravention or failure to comply, by the employer or a person on its behalf
      `the person is the employer` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the person asked about is the employer
      `the person is involved in the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc s 13(3): the person is involved, as ERA s 142W treats a person involved in a breach
      `the conduct occurred on` IS A DATE  @desc The date of the conduct (Schedule cl 2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`liable to a penalty under s 13` `there was a contravention or failure by or for the employer` `the person is the employer` `the person is involved in the contravention` `the conduct occurred on` MEANS
    IF `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` `the conduct occurred on`
    THEN     `there was a contravention or failure by or for the employer`
         AND (`the person is the employer` OR `the person is involved in the contravention`)
    ELSE `penalties for conduct before 1 April 2016 fall under s 13 as it stood before the 2016 Act, which this encoding does not carry`

@ref s 13; Schedule cl 2
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`penalties for conduct before 1 April 2016 fall under s 13 as it stood before the 2016 Act, which this encoding does not carry` MEANS
    REFUSE "penalties for conduct before 1 April 2016 fall under s 13 as it stood before the 2016 Act, which this encoding does not carry"

-- s 13(2) "A worker or a Labour Inspector may recover a penalty under
-- subsection (1), but the worker may recover a penalty only in relation to
-- the employer."
@ref s 13(2)
GIVEN claimant IS A Claimant, `against the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may recover a penalty under s 13` claimant `, against the employer:` `against the employer` IF
    CONSIDER claimant
    WHEN `a Labour Inspector` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the worker` THEN `against the employer`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 1: title; commencement 1 February 1984"
         "s 2: interpretation — read into the facts (employer, worker, wages, money, specified cheque, financial institution, local authority)"
         "ss 2A, 3: application of amendments; the Crown is bound"
         "s 6(4)(b): a group notice is valid for the worker it is given to"
         "ss 6(3)(ba) (second), 6(5), 14, 18(2): repealed"
         "s 18(1), s 19: administration; consequential repeals"
         "s 12A(3): a Labour Inspector's proceedings may be continued by another Inspector"
